# SPA fallback for the vendored concept sites (2026-11-21): each concept
# is a client-side-routed SPA, so a direct load / refresh / bookmark of a
# sub-route (e.g. /concepts/tally-bar/shop) must serve the SPA's index.html
# with a 200, not the main site's 404 page. Cloudflare Pages serves an
# existing static file before applying these rules, so real assets under
# /concepts/<slug>/assets/ are unaffected.
#
# The destination MUST be the directory URL (with trailing slash), NOT
# the index.html file: Pages 308-redirects any request for */index.html
# to its directory, so a rewrite to index.html can never serve the SPA —
# a static rule 308s, and a splat rule whose destination matches its own
# source 404s. The directory form serves the SPA's index with a 200.
# (Verified live 2026-11-21: /concepts/tally-bar/shop -> 200 SPA HTML.)
/concepts/tally-bar/*  /concepts/tally-bar/  200
/concepts/look-out-below/*  /concepts/look-out-below/  200
/concepts/stitch-and-tan/*  /concepts/stitch-and-tan/  200
/concepts/product-site/*  /concepts/product-site/  200
/concepts/portfolio-concept/*  /concepts/portfolio-concept/  200
